<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.3.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00404</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.3.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2126a9e8-c268-4eaa-83ab-b02599c1819b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will activate and build on what you have learned about solving by <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">substitution</term>, or replacing a variable with a number or
        with an expression. Various substitutions can be done to solve the same system. You will
        also begin to build an awareness of the kinds of systems that are conducive to being solved
        by substitution.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Solve systems of equations by substituting a variable or an expression.</item>
        <item>Know more than one way to perform a substitution and decide which way or what to
          substitute based on how the given equations are written.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>2.3.1: Finding Connections between Graphs and Equations</item>
        <item>2.3.2: Checking Solutions in Systems<list id="list-00003">
            <item>2.3.2: Self Check</item>
          </list>
    <list id="list-00004">
            <item>2.3.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>2.3.3: Solving Equations Using Substitution<list id="list-00005">
            <item>2.3.3: Self Check</item>
          </list>
    <list id="list-00006">
            <item>2.3.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>2.3.4: Solving More Equations</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00007">
        <item>2.3.5: Practice</item>
        <item>2.3.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
